config BR2_PACKAGE_ROCKNIX_JOYPAD
	bool "rocknix-joypad"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Out-of-tree input drivers for the gamepad controls of the
	  Rockchip handhelds: rocknix-joypad (multi-ADC sticks) and
	  rocknix-singleadc-joypad (one ADC multiplexed across the
	  sticks, as on the Game Console R36S and its clones). The
	  device tree picks the driver by compatible string; both are
	  built, and the kernel loads whichever matches.

	  https://github.com/ROCKNIX/rocknix-joypad

comment "rocknix-joypad needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
